The "All products" and "Bundles" headings on the products page are now in capitals, 16px, with 0.08em letter spacing.

**The change:** I added one rule to the Products section of `site/css/pages.css`:

```css
.page-products .section-title {
  font-size: 16px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}
```

The other pages use the same `section-title` class, so I limited the rule to the products page with the `page-products` class on its `<body>`. The rule also overrides the smaller mobile heading size (21px), so the headings stay at 16px on small screens too.

**Checked in a browser:**
- On the products page, both headings show as "ALL PRODUCTS" and "BUNDLES" at 16px with 1.28px letter spacing (0.08em) at 1280px and 400px widths.
- The home page section headings are unchanged (24px, normal case).
- All 16 functional tests pass.

`.idea/` and `.vscode/` folders now appear as untracked in git. I didn't create them, so I left them alone. Nothing is committed.

STATUS: DONE

